  "findings": [
    "All seven A/B keys reviewed in front, oblique, side and top. Head, arm, grip and broom tasks agree between A/B; existing geometry and facial identity remain recognizable.",
    "B reduces common lower-body turning relative to A; the belly pigment rotates progressively toward the chest and visible gray lower attachments remain near the planted paws.",
    "Four shaded whole-body/hip/ankle views for A, B, no-relative-turn and no-leg-anchor were inspected. B has a broad continuous twist without observed abrupt waist pinching, folds, cracks or new exposed gaps at these samples.",
    "The chest and lower-frame distinction is clearest in belly presentation and tail direction; the large head hides much of the upper torso in top view.",
    "The fixed club-arm roots remain concealed as in the original. B preserves the prior elbow/reach design; this is a controlled rig experiment, not a match of the complete generated broom excursion.",
    "No stepping, new face distortion, grip switching, second broom or abrupt bristle detachment is present in the pilot."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Generated front, oblique, side and top performances are independent; exact joints and force distribution are not measured.",
    "The test shares upper-chest/hand tasks between A/B deliberately. It cannot establish an improved final performance from lower-body differences alone.",
    "Existing simplified gray leg/paw overlap and arm-root embedding remain. Pilot appearance is not an all-state collision or surface certificate.",
    "Clay highlights are bright; oblique/side shading and silhouettes were inspected at native640px, but broader lighting and range qualification remain separate.",
    "No owner adoption, independent quality score or real-time skeletal export is claimed."
  ]
}
